From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gui: service Tcl's event queue while Qt runs the main loop

In GUI mode QApplication::exec() owns the main loop and nothing calls
Tcl_DoOneEvent, so a script's `after`, `fileevent` and `socket -server`
callbacks are registered and never run: `after 100 {puts hi}` returns a
handle and prints nothing. A Tcl server sourced into a GUI session, such
as a debug daemon answering queries over a socket, cannot work there.

A QTimer drains the queue every 50 ms on the Qt main thread, where
Tcl_Eval already runs, at most 32 events a tick so a callback that
reschedules itself cannot starve the UI.

Not upstreamed; retires at a bump onto an OpenROAD whose GUI services
the Tcl event loop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 openroad/gui/src/gui.cpp | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/openroad/gui/src/gui.cpp b/openroad/gui/src/gui.cpp
index c5e67f3..3497f65 100644
--- a/openroad/gui/src/gui.cpp
+++ b/openroad/gui/src/gui.cpp
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #include <QImage>
 #include <QPushButton>
 #include <QString>
+#include <QTimer>
 #include <QWidget>
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <any>
@@ -48,6 +49,7 @@
 #include "qtDialogs.h"
 #include "ruler.h"
 #include "scriptWidget.h"
+#include "tcl.h"
 #include "timingWidget.h"
 #include "utl/Logger.h"
 #include "utl/decode.h"
@@ -930,6 +932,18 @@ int startGui(int& argc,
   }
 
   if (do_exec) {
+    // Nothing else services Tcl's event queue while Qt owns the main loop, so
+    // after/fileevent/socket callbacks would never fire. Draining it from a
+    // QTimer keeps them on the Qt main thread, where Tcl_Eval already runs;
+    // the per-tick bound stops a self-rescheduling callback starving the UI.
+    QTimer tcl_event_pump;
+    QObject::connect(&tcl_event_pump, &QTimer::timeout, []() {
+      for (int i = 0; i < 32 && Tcl_DoOneEvent(TCL_ALL_EVENTS | TCL_DONT_WAIT);
+           ++i) {
+      }
+    });
+    tcl_event_pump.start(50);
+
     exit_code = QApplication::exec();
   }
 
